{"availability":"available","full":"Sahilll15/minutes","name":"minutes","description":"Record or upload a meeting and get minutes where every decision and action item links to the transcript line it came from.","category":"AI & machine learning","language":"TypeScript","stars":0,"forks":0,"created":"2026-10-02T22:35:19Z","updated":"2026-10-08T17:21:06Z","branch":"main","homepage":"https://minutes-sand.vercel.app","topics":["ai","nextjs","openai","speech-to-text","typescript","vercel"],"demo":"https://minutes-sand.vercel.app/","color":"#302e55","ink":"#dbd2ff","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-08T18:21:48.986Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-08T18:21:48.986Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-08T18:21:48.986Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-06T15:46:30.654Z","stars":0,"forks":0},{"at":"2026-10-08T18:21:48.986Z","stars":0,"forks":0}],"technologies":["Next.js"],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["Meeting minutes from recorded or uploaded audio, where every item links back to the transcript lines it came from.","Whoever writes up a meeting often has to show where each point came from: PMs, team leads, agency account managers. Minutes records a meeting in the browser or takes an upload and returns a 3 sentence summary, decisions, action items with owners and due dates, open questions and risks. Click an item and the transcript scrolls to those lines, highlights the quoted phrase and moves the audio there.","Two sample meetings ship in public/samples/ (a product standup and a client kickoff), so you can run the whole pipeline in one click."],"features":[],"sourceUrl":"https://github.com/Sahilll15/minutes/blob/main/README.md","fingerprint":"baa0b080fbd4675237e67a7e86f696d8e1e2018d297ee7551e38c03553f4cbb5","extractedAt":"2026-10-08T21:29:37.766Z"},"overviewCheckedAt":"2026-10-08T21:29:37.766Z","projectInsights":{"version":1,"whatItDoes":{"text":"Meeting minutes from recorded or uploaded audio, where every item links back to the transcript lines it came from.","sourceUrl":"https://g